{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fare on this trip is UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd of SGD 34.50 carried on the base_fare line and per_km_rate_sgd and per_min_rate_sgd both null, so the distance and time charges were fixed at booking. Under POL-RD-11 the distance-and-time refund route is closed: POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. The rider's request to 'refund the extra distance' therefore fails on the fare model alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Charged_total of SGD 39.00 exceeds the SGD 34.50 quote by exactly SGD 4.50, and that whole difference is ERP on the ledger. SGD 2.50 of it is the KPE (Defu Flyover) gantry, which the trip_record's own optimal-route source names as sitting on the optimal route, which carries on_optimal_route = true, and which the trace passes within 250 m; under POL-RD-09 it is a properly chargeable pass-through and is not refundable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.tolls_erp",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only gantry line that is not properly chargeable is the SGD 2.00 AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line: the trace never comes within 5.4 km of that gantry, so it fails the 250 m crossing test and is a billing-integrity failure refunded in full under POL-RD-09(4), available whether or not any deviation exists. The driver does not resist that single correction, and it is the full extent of the rider's recovery on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.erp_gantries",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On this trip's own trace the excess is 5.78 km over a 22.4 km optimal, or 25.8%. The driver does not dispute that this clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gate (over 20% and over 0.8 km), but it is far below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gate, so the deviation is not MATERIAL; POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not engaged and no POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the materiality gate were reached, no repeat-deviation pattern is established on the fields POL-RD-06 names: deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the threshold of 3, and 1 divided by 523 completed_trips_90d is 0.0019, below the 0.05 ratio. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a different field, is not the trailing-90-day figure the clause asks for, and may not be substituted for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only traffic artifact in the pool is EV-ADVIS-00115-01, which is MISSING — admissibility weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT of BLOCKING severity — and records that no LTA advisory covers the CTE, the KPE or the TPE in the 21:06-21:48 window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run for either side and the driver does not assert it; his heavy-traffic explanation stands unverified, and it makes no difference to the money, because POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges whether or not the diversion was justified.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00115-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-00115-01.admissibility.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log shows the driver told the rider before the diversion that he was going KPE then TPE and the rider replied 'ok'. That is disclosure, not a rider instruction — the message is the driver's, not the rider's, and no waypoint_hint is recorded — so the driver does not claim POL-RD-04 exoneration for any part of the excess; the point is only that the route was announced in advance rather than concealed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
